{title: As with Gladness Men of Old}
{artist: William Dix & Conrad Kocher}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[G]As with gladness [C]men of [G]old [C]did the [G]guiding [D]star be[G]hold,
as with joy they [C]hailed its [G]light, [C]leading [G]onward, [D]beaming [G]bright —
so, most gracious [D]Lord, may [Em]we [C]ever[G]more be [D]led to [G]thee.

Verse 2
As with
joyful steps they sped
To that lowly manger bed
There to
bend the knee before
Him whom Heav'n and earth adore;
So may we with willing feet
Ever seek Thy mercy seat.

Verse 3
As they
offered gifts most rare
At that manger rude and bare;
So may
we with holy joy,
Pure and free from sin's alloy,
All our costliest treasures bring,
Christ, to Thee, our heav'nly King.

Verse 4
Holy Jesus, ev'ry day
Keep us in the narrow way;
And, when
earthly things are past,
Bring our ransomed souls at last
Where they need no star to guide,
Where no clouds Thy glory hide.

Verse 5
In the
heav'nly country bright,
Need they no created light;
Thou its
Light, its Joy, its Crown,
Thou its Sun which goes not down;
There forever may we sing
Alleluias to our King!
